SUBJECT: Software Engineering | UNIT: 2 | TOPIC: SINGLE INHERITANCE IN JAVA

Exercise - 4 Aim: 4a) Write a JAVA program to implement single Inheritance
Program:
class A {
  int a, b;
  void show() {
    System.out.println("The values of A and B: " + a + "," + b);
  }
}
class B extends A {
  int c;
  void display() {
    System.out.println("The values of C: " + c);
  }
  void sum() {
    System.out.println("The values of a+b+c: " + (a + b + c));
  }
}
class SingleInh {
  public static void main(String args[]) {
    A a1 = new A();
    a1.a = 10;
    a1.b = 20;
    System.out.println("Content of superclass object only");
    a1.show();
    B b1 = new B();
    b1.a = 1;
    b1.b = 2;
    b1.c = 3;
    System.out.println("Content of subclass object only");
    b1.show();
    b1.display();
    b1.sum();
  }
}

